Keeps a link parameter from replacing the prototype of the parsed link or from reading inherited
properties. The parser assigns every parameter and treats any truthy value of `ref[attr]` as an
earlier occurrence, so `__proto__="a"` sets the prototype of the link to
`[Object.prototype, 'a']`, and `constructor=x` gives `constructor: [Object, 'x']`. Now only an own
property counts as an earlier occurrence, and a `__proto__` parameter becomes an own property, also
in the copies that `expandRelations` makes for each relation, which used `Object.assign`. The
latest release (1.1.4) still has this bug.

